{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1285831-a-question-about-aiming","id":1285831,"title":"A Question about Aiming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-08T01:56:29-08:00","id":1285831,"title":"A Question about Aiming","content":"The Edge Sniper 1 Dead Calm says: &quot;Double the Enhancement your character gains from taking the time to carefully aim an attack.&quot;<br /> <br /> I am unsure how that works.<br /> <br /> Do i double the Enhancment Bonus of the Weapon?<br /> I haven't found a Stunt that involves aiming, that would give such an enhancement bonus.<br /> <br /> Maybe i missed something in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3050-lilliane","name":"Lilliane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T02:18:50-08:00","id":1285835,"title":"","content":"I looked for it too, with no results. It looks like one of those GM choices.<br /> I would add a +1 Enhancement to aiming any shot if you spend one turn aiming. If the gun is a long gun and have a scope you get a +2. Snipers double it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T02:12:47-08:00","id":1289854,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a>: Thank you i will use that.<br /> <br /> But i would also like to have an offical answer to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3050-lilliane","name":"Lilliane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-20T05:53:33-08:00","id":1289881,"title":"","content":"Another option that may be interesting is a dinamic bonus, you take a action to aim, roll Aim + Cunning to check the environment difficulty equals to the difficulty of a regular attack against the target. Any additional success are added as Enhancements on the proper shot, as if you were using the Feint Stunt. It may be a more elegant way to make sure a trained shooter that can understand the environment takes more advantage of the action.<br /> <br /> I, as a untrained, could spend an entire afternoon aiming with no better result on my final shot, but a sniper would do much better by spending a few extra seconds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T13:37:46-08:00","id":1291592,"title":"","content":"Not a bad idea, but i am a little scared about doubling it, with the edge.<br /> <br /> That might become too powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3050-lilliane","name":"Lilliane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T00:45:05-08:00","id":1291739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilliane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1285831-a-question-about-aiming#post1285831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Edge Sniper 1 Dead Calm says: &amp;quot;Double the Enhancement your character gains from taking the time to carefully aim an attack.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I am unsure how that works.<br /> <br /> Do i double the Enhancment Bonus of the Weapon?<br /> I haven't found a Stunt that involves aiming, that would give such an enhancement bonus.<br /> <br /> Maybe i missed something in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a house rule, but what I use is each action spent aiming gives +1 Enhancement, up to a number of turns equal to the character\u2019s Aim skill. Sniper doubles the bonus per turn, with the same turn limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T06:22:15-08:00","id":1294376,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for your answers. I will give it a try with my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3050-lilliane","name":"Lilliane","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-06T07:02:02-08:00","id":1294380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1285831-a-question-about-aiming?p=1291739#post1291739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a house rule, but what I use is each action spent aiming gives +1 Enhancement, up to a number of turns equal to the character\u2019s Aim skill. Sniper doubles the bonus per turn, with the same turn limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you also top it out at +3 Enhancement as the recommended normal maximum enhancement, with +5 being on the extreme side and the absolute max not counting scale?<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T01:44:56-08:00","id":1294640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1285831-a-question-about-aiming?p=1294380#post1294380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you also top it out at +3 Enhancement as the recommended normal maximum enhancement, with +5 being on the extreme side and the absolute max not counting scale?</div> </div> </div> </div>No I don\u2019t, I let each round add +1 up to the dots in Aim. I double the final bonus with Sniper. The reasoning is firstly that it\u2019s an Edge - a player wanted to take it and they want to get good, fun use out of it, so I let them. Secondly, each round they want to spend doing nothing but aiming is a round they\u2019re doing nothing but aiming. I figure that patience in setting up what they want deserves a reward in itself. Also, while I recall that Scion calls out +3 Enhancement as recommended maximum, I don\u2019t remember Trinity Continuum doing the same. (Feel free to correct me if I\u2019ve missed the reference.) I see this as a strength of the Storypath system, that it\u2019s scalable and adaptable to different settings and expectations through adjusting the various dials.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019d also make clear that I believe the Sniper question came up in errata and my current take is just a house rule until the errata are incorporated. Once that\u2019s done I\u2019ll use whatever the system says there. \ud83d\ude42","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T03:46:37-08:00","id":1294664,"title":"","content":"My initial reaction is the +1 per round aiming feels very CoD and higher health track. I would think the final may be aim +1 (sniper+2) or aim/gear-scope +2 (sniper +3 or +4) which still hits the core mechanic <br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:30:53-08:00","id":1294675,"title":"","content":"My idea is still Aim + Cunning against the target every round to gain enhancements, but never more than aim skill. Sniper doubles it. If miss the test loses all the staked enhancements... it\u2019s not a matter of sitting and waiting, you are preparing the gun to shoot in the exact moment, and you can lose the timing, a leaf can fall just in front of the scope, you may get distracted by another possible target, I don\u2019t know... and you get momentum if you miss the aiming test, what\u2019s fair...<br /> <br /> Gear scope works different, it allows the shooter to have one extra preferential range band, so a assault rifle is Designed for close range, with a scope it gets Medium range (100m with no penalty). You can have a Long reach sniper rifle with range bands of medium (30 to 100m) and long (100m to 1km), allowing a quite long shot with no penalties, but lacking the precision for short range shoots...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:10:07-08:00","id":1294721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1285831-a-question-about-aiming?p=1294664#post1294664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial reaction is the +1 per round aiming feels very CoD and higher health track. I would think the final may be aim +1 (sniper+2) or aim/gear-scope +2 (sniper +3 or +4) which still hits the core mechanic<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div>Except aren't you doing a max of two injuries? One for the do damage enhancement and one for the critical hit enhancement? All those extra successes could be used buy off difficulties like range, cover, darkness, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T11:58:01-08:00","id":1294810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1285831-a-question-about-aiming?p=1294721#post1294721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except aren't you doing a max of two injuries? One for the do damage enhancement and one for the critical hit enhancement? All those extra successes could be used buy off difficulties like range, cover, darkness, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct. You\u2019re not one-shotting major characters. You\u2019ll put them in a bad situation and set them up for your allies.<br /> <br /> (Unless scale comes into it, but the errata team are clarifying when scale applies as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 03-07-2019, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}